<title>HONG KONG: Fan, Moore leave Hongkong Telecom board.</title>
<headline>Fan, Moore leave Hongkong Telecom board.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong Telecommunications Ltd said on Tuesday that Henry Fan and Vernon Moore had resigned as non-executive directors of the company as from June 6.</p>
<p>The move follows the completion of the sale by CITIC Pacific Ltd of its entire 7.74 percent stake in Hongkong Telecom to China Everbright Holdings Co Ltd. Fan is managing director of CITIC Pacific and Moore is deputy managing director.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6441</p>
</text>
